    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 30th August 2006, the retention of a single storey rear extension, with dimensions 2.26m wide, 7.02m deep, and 3.61m high, returning a volume of 57.27m3, giving a total volume increase to the original house of 57.27m3, as shown on drawing numbers 460/001 - 460/007, received 30th August 2006, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the development consisting of the retention of a single storey rear extension, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n\r\n\r\n"
